          "You never made those seeking your favor travel to you — rather, your bounty came to them, brought as fine imported gifts by the noblest of bringers.",
          "Knowing well that traveling itself brings hardship, and that the bitterest profit of all is the profit gained through forced migration.",
          "Yet you would burden me with the terror of travel and its demon dangers, companion of a winter that shrivels the very knuckles of my fingers.",
          "Especially when the water dons its own proud armor of ice, and disrupts the very breathing of the east wind and the south wind.",
          "A biting frost snarls at whoever ventures across the land, its harm touching him even without any wrapping of turban-cloth to shield him.",
          "As though the whole of true affection, and all of praise, meant nothing but a young man's plunging into the sea, or crossing the open wastelands.",
          "By my life — if you reckon my reward against me by lowering it, then you have simply followed the habit of any ordinary accountant.",
          "Have mercy — I am certain that you are a secretary whose own rank rises above every other secretary.",
          "So spare me the rules of chancery prose — they are the enemy of the rules of poetry, never coming close to them at all.",
          "Otherwise, no one acting justly would ever pit the most serious of the serious against the most playful of the playful, as equals.",
          "Could the thought ever truly escape you, of rewarding me by letting me stay settled, spared the hardship of seeking further?",
          "Then you and I would both be found, standing between a pure act of favor and pure praise, unmixed with any reproach.",
          "And you would step outside the harsh judgments of those who have grown so strict that they have turned their own blessings into calamities.",
          "Could this possibly escape you, O son of Muḥammad, when you yourself are the refuge in every pressing, weighty matter?",
          "Yours are sound judgment and generosity — both of these together stand as guarantors, able to lift away even the most crushing disasters.",
          "You have always been a guiding star's light for the drought-struck and the bewildered, until people said you were one of the very stars yourself.",
          "You come to the rescue and guide the way, amid drought and confusion, with abundant plenty and a piercingly bright radiance.",
          "The finest of favors is one my own hand has not yet reached — though my raven, at least, has not yet croaked of parting.",
          "I see that whenever you reward me amid ease, it is as though you were leading a whole kingdom to me, escorted by troops.",
          "And whenever you reward me amid hardship instead, I see you then in the guise of one who both rewards and punishes at once.",
          "And if kindness did not include both a pure, pleasant kind and a troubled, murky kind — for kindness comes from many different sources —",
          "— then the most exalted in rank among the great poets would never have uttered his verse about the Ghassānid kings of mingled lineage.",
          "I owe 'Amr blessing after blessing, and to his father as well — blessings that carry no scorpion's sting within them.",
          "And no scorpion is more cunning than separation itself — its sting strikes right between the ribs and the breastbone.",
          "And it was precisely his dread of separation that inspired his own famous line: \"Leave me, O Umayma, to my exhausting grief.\"",
          "You refuse anything less than burdening your own kindness with a purity free of any harmful taint.",
          "Rather, true glory itself refuses anything but your own high price, and your rising above the mountain-peak of the calculating giver.",
          "So bear patiently the burden of carrying the whole weight yourself, even though loading it is hard, even for the mightiest of camels.",
