          "For whoever leads a people, his own excellence obliges that he be seen striving even for their lowliest member, even while they themselves are still at play.",
          "And whoever never ceases climbing the steep ascent of glory, however difficult the climb, attains the very highest of ranks.",
          "Have you not seen how I have exhausted my own mind, polishing this poem for you, only so that I might not be afflicted with more hardship?",
          "I have granted you an ornament of praise, as though it were the very longing of every lover for the embrace of his beloved.",
          "Elegant, truly deserving that its small caskets be made of pearl — no, rather, of the very breasts of young maidens themselves.",
          "And you deserve it well — if you reward me for it, I will give you even more; and if you hold back, I will remain without reproach.",
          "For if a group of people should ever ask me about you, I will testify against myself, admitting my own poor conduct.",
          "I will say: he invited me toward his generosity, so I came to it — yet he did not withhold it, but scattered it instead among the plunderers.",
          "His bounty never once shut itself off from me behind any barrier, nor did it ever hide itself from me there behind any chamberlain.",
          "But it presented itself openly, while I turned aside toward my own trade — so it returned, without injustice, back to the finest of all givers.",
          "I have said nothing about you but the truth, and you have never ceased walking a clear, well-trodden path of glory's own tradition.",
          "And I would be the most wretched of men, if my own garment were buttoned up over the sin of a liar and the grief of one utterly disappointed.",
          "You have always been the free-born young man whose very character wards off the edge of claws from other free men.",
          "You are not like the one who runs about, whose very words carry both the complaint of a robbed man and the aggression of a robber, at once.",
          "Such a man seeks the good favor of others, and if they refuse it, he attacks their honor, snarling like a pack of hounds.",
