          "But as for a young man gifted with wisdom and eloquence, demand of him instead sound judgment amid the company of speakers.",
          "Reward me, grant me ease, and make my recompense abundant, and persist steadily in the flow of your kindness toward me.",
          "So that your generosity may reach me whole, entirely free of fault, with nothing in it for any faultfinder to seize upon.",
          "I make my own boldness heavier, so that you may bear its weight willingly, as one who is pleased, not resentfully, as one who is angered.",
          "Seeking a pleasant gift is no strange innovation, nor is the wonder felt by those who seek such gifts anything to marvel at.",
          "All of that is only further increase to your own high standing, and to the truthfulness of these flowing, striking verses of mine.",
          "And it is not right to diminish the one who seeks increase from you, especially when your wealth is as abundant as a great herd of milk-camels.",
          "And you are the one whose least gift, come morning, is already the fulfillment of every wish — indeed, the satisfaction of every need.",
          "The hopes of those who come to you are weighed out against wealth itself, while others merely support their people with false hopes.",
          "I have stayed on so that your blessings might grow blessing upon blessing, and so you might be enriched with a fresh face, never a pale one.",
          "And so that no one who speaks might say he both rewarded him and punished him at once — for talk branches out in every possible direction.",
          "My guarding your kindness against disgrace demands your further increase in gifts to me, O son of noble governors.",
          "Through your own face, every single thing has come to be illuminated, and shows a smiling face, never a scowling one.",
          "So do not squander it unjustly on occasions of anger — for you were never given a face like that one merely to be used for anger.",
          "You have spread across the world a radiance that illuminated it, when once it was a darkness of the deepest, most impenetrable gloom.",
          "It is as though you, facing all of creation, were the very rising-points of a sun that dawned upon its own setting-places.",
          "May it please any young man who praised you, that he obtained his wish from you, and that he never carried the burden of a liar's sin.",
          "God's own pleasure lies within those very saddlebags, along with wealth, all together — so what a triumph awaits those saddlebags!",
